{"name":"Cannon Ball","hex":"#484335","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cannon ball","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of cannonball."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cannon_ball"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cannonball (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cannonball is a 1976 comedy film directed by Paul Bartel and starring David Carradine. The film is co-produced by the American studios Cross-County Productions and Harbour Productions and Hong Kong's Shaw Brothers Studio. It is one of two released in 1976 that were based on the Cannonball Baker Sea-to-Shining-Sea Memorial Trophy Dash, a real illegal cross-continent road race that took place for a number of years in the United States. The same topic later became the basis for the films The Cannonball Run, Cannonball Run II and Speed Zone. The film was written and directed by Paul Bartel, who also directed Death Race 2000."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/19/CannonballPoster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cannonball_(film)"},{"title":"Cannonball (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Cannonball is a British/Canadian adventure drama series starring Paul Birch and William Campbell, and aired on CBC Television in Canada, ABC Weekend TV in the United Kingdom, and in syndication in the United States. Produced by Normandie Productions and ITC Entertainment, the series' interiors were filmed at Canadian Film Industries Limited, a studio in Canada. Exteriors were shot in and around Toronto."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cannonball_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Cannon Ball (roller coaster)","blocks":[{"text":"Cannon Ball is a wooden roller coaster located at Lake Winnepesaukah amusement park in Rossville, Georgia, United States. The ride opened in 1967, was designed by John C. Allen, and was built by Philadelphia Toboggan Coasters. It is one of three roller coasters at the park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/The_Cannon_Ball_-_Lake_Winnepesaukah_Amusement_Park_-_Lakeview%2C_Georgia.jpg/330px-The_Cannon_Ball_-_Lake_Winnepesaukah_Amusement_Park_-_Lakeview%2C_Georgia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cannon_Ball_(roller_coaster)"},{"title":"Cannon","blocks":[{"text":"A cannon is a large-caliber gun classified as a type of artillery, which usually launches a projectile using explosive chemical propellant. Gunpowder was the primary propellant before the invention of smokeless powder during the late 19th century. Cannons vary in gauge, effective range, mobility, rate of fire, angle of fire and firepower; different forms of cannon combine and balance these attributes in varying degrees, depending on their intended use on the battlefield. A cannon is a type of heavy artillery weapon. The word cannon is derived from several languages, in which the original definition can usually be translated as tube, cane, or reed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/%28Saint-Lys%29_Fauconneau_de_1589.jpg/330px-%28Saint-Lys%29_Fauconneau_de_1589.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cannon"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Yuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg/500px-Yuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Yuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg/1280px-Yuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Yuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg/500px-Yuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bronze cannon with inscription dated the 3rd year of the Zhiyuan era (1332) of the Yuan dynasty (1271–1368); it was discovered at the Yunju Temple of Fangshan District, Beijing in 1935.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Ming_Dynasty_field_artillery_cannon.jpg/500px-Ming_Dynasty_field_artillery_cannon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Ming_Dynasty_field_artillery_cannon.jpg/500px-Ming_Dynasty_field_artillery_cannon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bronze \"thousand ball thunder cannon\" from the Huolongjing.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMing_Dynasty_field_artillery_cannon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/EarlyCannonDeNobilitatibusSapientiiEtPrudentiisRegumManuscriptWalterdeMilemete1326.jpg/500px-EarlyCannonDeNobilitatibusSapientiiEtPrudentiisRegumManuscriptWalterdeMilemete1326.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/EarlyCannonDeNobilitatibusSapientiiEtPrudentiisRegumManuscriptWalterdeMilemete1326.jpg/1280px-EarlyCannonDeNobilitatibusSapientiiEtPrudentiisRegumManuscriptWalterdeMilemete1326.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/EarlyCannonDeNobilitatibusSapientiiEtPrudentiisRegumManuscriptWalterdeMilemete1326.jpg/500px-EarlyCannonDeNobilitatibusSapientiiEtPrudentiisRegumManuscriptWalterdeMilemete1326.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Earliest picture of a European cannon, \"De Nobilitatibus Sapientii Et Prudentiis Regum\", Walter de Milemete, 1326","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarlyCannonDeNobilitatibusSapientiiEtPrudentiisRegumManuscriptWalterdeMilemete1326.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Copper_alloy_bombard_Grodno.jpg/500px-Copper_alloy_bombard_Grodno.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Copper_alloy_bombard_Grodno.jpg/500px-Copper_alloy_bombard_Grodno.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Reconstruction of a copper alloy cannon from Grodno, late 14th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACopper_alloy_bombard_Grodno.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Siege_orleans.jpg/500px-Siege_orleans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Siege_orleans.jpg/1280px-Siege_orleans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Siege_orleans.jpg/500px-Siege_orleans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two cannons featuring in a miniature from 1484 depicting the siege of Orléans in 1429","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASiege_orleans.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/%C5%A0ibenik_-_topovi.jpg/500px-%C5%A0ibenik_-_topovi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/%C5%A0ibenik_-_topovi.jpg/1280px-%C5%A0ibenik_-_topovi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/%C5%A0ibenik_-_topovi.jpg/500px-%C5%A0ibenik_-_topovi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cannon from the 15th century at Šibenik city walls","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%C5%A0ibenik_-_topovi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https:/